 The BFD 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios. Stock: Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Anthropic this morning launched the roadshow for an IPO that could raise up to $62.5 billion at a market cap just north of $1 trillion.

 Why it's the BFD: This is smaller than expected, despite what would be eye-popping numbers for most any other company.

 By the numbers: Anthropic plans to sell 801.4 million shares at $70-$78 per share. That works out to $56 billion to $62.5 billion raised, at a market cap of between $916 billion and $1.02 trillion.

 The high end of Anthropic's fully diluted valuation would be around $1.4 trillion. There's also a greenshoe that could raise an additional $8.66 billion to $9.65 billion and a concurrent $26 billion private placement to Google, Nvidia, AMD, Broadcom, Micron, Microsoft, and TSMC. Altogether, the IPO could generate over $98 billion in proceeds. For context: Anthropic was valued at $965 billion in its most recent private round. The apples-to-apples comparison would be with the fully diluted value.

 SpaceX raised $75 billion in its IPO and a total of $86.25 billion with the exercised greenshoe. The bottom line: Expect Anthropic shares to begin trading next Wednesday or Thursday.

 
 
